# Line endings.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf on, so a working-copy
# file is CRLF while the stored blob is LF. That is fine for Python and
# TypeScript, and fatal for anything a Linux kernel has to execute: a shell
# script with CRLF fails as `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r: No such file or directory`,
# which reads as a missing interpreter rather than as a line-ending problem and
# has cost people entire evenings.
#
# These are the files that cross to Linux and must stay LF regardless of the
# platform they were last edited on.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
Caddyfile       text eol=lf
env.template    text eol=lf
